 ## slugify

-`slugify(text, sep='-')` lowercases the words of `text` and joins them with `sep`.
+`slugify(text, sep='-', max_length=None)` lowercases the words of `text` and joins
+them with `sep`. Set `max_length` to limit the result to the longest prefix of
+whole words that fits, without a trailing separator. If the first word is too
+long, it is cut to `max_length` characters. `None` leaves the length unlimited.
+Values below 1 raise `ValueError`, including for empty text.

 ```python
 >>> from strkit import slugify
 >>> slugify('Hello, World!')
 'hello-world'
+>>> slugify('Hello World Again', max_length=12)
+'hello-world'
+>>> slugify('Supercalifragilistic word', max_length=5)
+'super'
 ```

 ## split_words

 `split_words(text)` returns the alphanumeric words of `text`.
+
+## truncate_at_boundary
+
+`truncate_at_boundary(slug, max_length, sep)` applies the same length limit to
+an existing slug. A slug that already fits is returned unchanged. Otherwise it
+keeps the longest prefix of whole `sep`-separated words that fits, with no
+trailing separator, or cuts the first word if necessary. Values below 1 raise
+`ValueError`. An empty separator provides no word boundaries, so an overlong
+slug is cut to `max_length` characters.
+
+```python
+>>> from strkit import truncate_at_boundary
+>>> truncate_at_boundary('hello::world::again', 12, '::')
+'hello::world'
+```
